 Math                                   
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 
                                        
 Inline math sits on the line: E = mc², 
 and α × β, and the subscripted aᵢⱼ     
 beside the flat a_{bc} that Unicode    
 cannot lower.                          
                                        
 Scripts that exist are raised: xⁿ⁺¹,   
 and e⁻ˣ raises the minus sign too.     
 Scripts that do not are written flat:  
 x^q.                                   
                                        
 Structures are linearised inline: a/b, 
 √x, and ∑ᵢ₌₁ⁿ i.                       
                                        
 Display math is drawn as box art:      
                                        
                  ┌─────────            
                  │  2                  
           −b ± ‾╲│ b  − 4ac            
           ─────────────────            
                  2a                    
                                        
 Currency is not math: it costs $5 and  
 $10 in total.                          
                                        
 Display: a fraction                    
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                    ┌─────────          
                    │  2                
             −b ± ‾╲│ b  − 4ac          
         x = ─────────────────          
                    2a                  
                                        
 Display: limits on a big operator      
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
        n    2   n(n + 1)(2n + 1)       
        ∑   i  = ────────────────       
      i = 1             6               
                                        
 Display: tall delimiters               
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                 ╭ a ╮2                 
                 │ ─ │                  
                 ╰ b ╯                  
                                        
 Display: an indexed root               
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                3 ─────                 
                √ x + 1                 
                                        
 Display: a formula wider than forty    
 columns                                
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 ╭ math ──────────────────────────────╮ 
 │ f(x) = a_0 + a_1 x + a_2 x^2 + a_› │ 
 ╰ this formula needs 43 columns ─────╯ 
                                        
 Display: a block that only defines     
 macros                                 
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 That block draws nothing and leaves no 
 gap behind it. What it defined is in   
 scope for every formula after it,      
 inline — 1/2 — and displayed:          
                                        
                   1   1                
               x = ─ + ─                
                   2   2                
                                        
 Display: a mixed block keeps its       
 macros to itself                       
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                 ℕ ⊂ ℤ                  
                                        
 Outside that block $\N$ is undefined,  
 so it reaches the reader as its        
 source.                                
                                        
 Display: a double bar stretched around 
 a fraction                             
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                 ║ a ║                  
                 ║ ─ ║                  
                 ║ b ║                  
                                        
 Display: a double bar around a single  
 row                                    
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                  ‖x‖                   
                                        
 Display: a binomial coefficient, which 
 has no inline form                     
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
                 ╭ n ╮                  
                 │   │                  
                 ╰ k ╯                  
                                        
 Written inline, $\binom{n}{k}$ reaches 
 the reader as its source too.          
                                        
